# Template for ai-service.env (a secret file, mode 600). install.sh creates
# ai-service.env from this file when it is missing, and asks for each API key
# whose line is empty. run.sh sources ai-service.env with bash, so keep to
# plain KEY=value lines and put single quotes around any value with spaces, $
# or parentheses (inside double quotes, bash still expands $).
# Restart the service after an edit.

# --- secrets ---
# Providers for /api/transcribe: set one, two or all three. At least one is
# required, or the service refuses to start. With more than one, a tray icon
# (macOS menu bar / Linux status area) opens a picker; the service starts on
# Groq and remembers the last choice in data/cache.db.
# Groq key (whisper-large-v3-turbo).
GROQ_API_KEY=
# AssemblyAI key for Universal-3.5 Pro on /api/transcribe, through the Sync
# API (sync.assemblyai.com). It accepts comart's WebM directly, so it needs no
# ffmpeg.
ASSEMBLYAI_API_KEY=
# OpenRouter key for MAI-Transcribe-2 on BOTH /api/transcribe and
# /api/transcribe-verbatim. Separate from OPENROUTER_API_KEY below (that one is
# /api/explain's) so each route can keep its own key. Needs ffmpeg on PATH:
# comart records WebM, and every mic clip is converted to WAV first.
OPENROUTER_TRANSCRIBE_API_KEY=
# Key for /api/explain: fill in EXACTLY ONE of the next two and leave the other
# empty. The service refuses to start with both set, so a request can never go
# to a model you did not expect.
# OpenRouter key for word explanations (not transcription).
OPENROUTER_API_KEY=
# Claude Platform key (api.anthropic.com).
CLAUDE_API_KEY=
# Key for /api/memoir/check: fill in EXACTLY ONE of the next two and leave the other
# empty. The service refuses to start with both set. Every Memoir variable
# starts with MEMOIR_, because the plain CLAUDE_API_KEY above is /api/explain's.
# Claude Platform key (api.anthropic.com).
MEMOIR_CLAUDE_API_KEY=
# Cerebras key. (Before 2026-10-20 this was called CEREBRAS_API_KEY; the old
# name makes the service refuse to start.)
MEMOIR_CEREBRAS_API_KEY=

# --- transcription ---
GROQ_MODEL=whisper-large-v3-turbo
# OpenRouter serves microsoft/mai-transcribe-2 with the same $0.10/hour price.
# /api/transcribe-verbatim asks for verbose_json + word timestamps + Azure's
# verbatim style, and OpenRouter caps Azure-backed uploads at 25 MB.
# Model id and endpoint are fixed in internal/server/openrouter.go.

# --- /api/explain model ---
# Model id for the provider whose key is set above. Leave it unset for the
# default: google/gemini-3.8-flash on OpenRouter, claude-opus-5-5 on Claude. With
# a Claude key the id must start with "claude-", or the service refuses to start.
#EXPLAIN_MODEL=
# OpenRouter only: thinking budget in tokens (reasoning.max_tokens). Thinking is
# never shown to the user.
EXPLAIN_REASONING_TOKENS=1024
# Claude only: thinking effort, low | medium | high | xhigh | max. It is the only
# thinking control Claude models take. Default: medium.
#EXPLAIN_EFFORT=medium

# --- /api/memoir/check model ---
# Model id for the provider whose key is set above. Leave it unset for the
# default: claude-opus-5-5 on Claude, qwen-3.8-27b on Cerebras. With a Claude
# key the id must start with "claude-", or the service refuses to start.
#MEMOIR_MODEL=
# Claude only: thinking effort, low | medium | high | xhigh | max. Default: medium.
#MEMOIR_EFFORT=medium
# Cerebras only: low | medium | high, or none to turn reasoning off. Keep it on:
# without reasoning Qwen breaks the JSON contract and edits text it must leave
# alone.
MEMOIR_REASONING_EFFORT=medium

# --- server ---
# The clients and install.sh's health check expect exactly this address.
LISTEN_ADDR=127.0.0.1:8770

# --- paths: leave unset ---
# run.sh defaults it relative to this folder, so the folder can move without an
# edit. On Linux the service may only write data/ and logs/, so keep it inside
# data/.
# Default: <repo>/data/cache.db (the Merriam-Webster cache).
#CACHE_DB=
